<%#
  TOOL OUTPUT (stage 3, S3-1) — every file inside the folder that an addon produced, listed ONCE
  here rather than inside whichever real subfolder it happens to sit in
  (_file_tree_section.html.erb filters @generated_ids out of every section for exactly this).
  @generated is { node_id => Maker::AddonState } (ProjectsController#show, one query pair for the
  whole page — Maker::AddonOrigin.for's own contract, CLAUDE.md §14a); @addon_origins already
  resolved each state's OWN addon page for the right-click menu every tile on this page carries, so
  this reads that hash rather than asking the Registry a second time (AddonOrigins#addon_origins_for
  is the one place that fetches it, and only once addon output is confirmed to exist at all).

  ALWAYS OPEN, LIKE LINKED — these are files that exist and are exactly where they should be; there
  is nothing here to fold away by default.

  TILES: the ordinary thumbnail (_file_tile.html.erb, reused so this is not a second copy of the
  seven-key wire contract) plus an ALWAYS-VISIBLE meta line underneath naming the saved item and
  its revision, and an "Open in <tool>" link when this deployment still serves that addon (nil when
  it does not — the same rule the file page's own button follows, docs/invariants/addons.md). LIST:
  _file_rows.html.erb, whose Origin column is never blank for a row that reached this group.

  Local: view (one of Maker::Project::VIEWS) — the FILES panel's, since that is the only panel this
  cross-cutting group renders in. Required since 2026-09-08: the page-wide `@view` cookie retired
  when the view became per panel (spec decision 6).
%>
<section class="attachment-group generated-group">
  <details open>
    <summary class="attachment-group-head">
      Generated <span class="muted">(<%= @generated.size %>)</span>
    </summary>
    <%# THE LISTING'S OWN ROW, NOT @page_nodes — @generated is scoped to @listing.node_ids, so
        @listing.row_for already carries this node's real Row, section and all, with no second
        lookup. @page_nodes is built from attachments/photos/BOM lines and has no reason to hold a
        plain folder file nothing ever attached. %>
    <% rows = @generated.filter_map { |node_id, state|
         row = @listing.row_for(node_id)
         [ row, state ] if row
       } %>
    <% if view == "list" %>
      <%= render "file_rows", rows: rows.map(&:first) %>
    <% else %>
      <div class="attachments-grid">
        <% rows.each do |row, state| %>
          <%# A plain wrapper, NOT a second .attachment-tile: _file_tile.html.erb already renders
              its own complete tile div, and doubling the class on an ENCLOSING element would put
              two elements answering to the same selector one inside the other, for no reason —
              the meta line below is a sibling, not part of the tile. %>
          <div class="generated-tile">
            <%= render "file_tile", row: row %>
            <div class="generated-meta">
              <span class="muted"><%= state.name %> · rev <%= state.revision %></span>
              <% if (origin = @addon_origins[row.node_id]) %>
                <%= link_to origin[:label], origin[:url], class: "linkbtn small" %>
              <% end %>
            </div>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </details>
</section>
